WEBVTT

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:14.896
Here we go, maro!

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:23.870
Fire Crisis!

00:02:29.033 --> 00:02:31.603
What happened to Homeron?!
Where's his ship?!

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.870
It crashed somewhere down there!

00:02:37.533 --> 00:02:42.433
PURSUIT OF THE DEVIL

00:02:44.766 --> 00:02:45.766
Hand me a wrench!

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:46.770
Right!

00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.070
What?!

00:02:59.333 --> 00:03:00.733
Are they retreating?!

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:06.370
It appears the Grankingdom fleet
has given up on the invasion

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:08.700
of our nation of Sabaru
and is withdrawing.

00:03:10.766 --> 00:03:13.126
However, there has been
significant damage to our ships

00:03:13.166 --> 00:03:14.666
and we are low on ammunition.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:16.230
The sun will be setting soon as well.

00:03:16.466 --> 00:03:17.726
It kills me to say this,

00:03:17.766 --> 00:03:20.926
but I recommend we give up
on a pursuit and reorganize our fleet.

00:03:22.766 --> 00:03:24.466
Turn us around 90 degrees to the right.

00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:30.103
We shall return to base after verifying that
the Grankingdom has actually withdrawn.

00:03:32.233 --> 00:03:34.503
Kluke! Isn't it fixed yet?!

00:03:34.966 --> 00:03:40.266
It's still only operating at 50% power.
I've got to get it up to 80%.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:43.070
Even as we speak,
Homeron could be...

00:03:43.333 --> 00:03:44.703
He could be dead, maro.

00:03:44.733 --> 00:03:46.003
Stop the nonsense!

00:03:46.333 --> 00:03:48.533
This isn't the time to
be worried about others.

00:03:49.533 --> 00:03:50.533
Look at that!

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:03.430
Yikes, maro!

00:04:03.533 --> 00:04:05.703
Are they going to shoot us down
along with their allies, maro?!

00:04:06.366 --> 00:04:07.366
Get in, everyone!

00:04:07.566 --> 00:04:09.326
What? But it's not fixed yet!

00:04:09.633 --> 00:04:11.733
We'll get nailed if we stay here!

00:04:19.333 --> 00:04:22.503
Rat-tat-tat-tat-tat-tat.
No, that'd never work, maro...

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:30.270
Please! Fly!

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:43.230
We're going down!

00:04:56.366 --> 00:04:58.466
Where did we end up crashing?

00:04:59.066 --> 00:05:02.696
According to the last verified coordinates,
we're near the border of both nations,

00:05:02.733 --> 00:05:06.233
southeast of Sabaru and
northwest of the Grankingdom.

00:05:06.833 --> 00:05:08.703
This is the Great Forest of Brandish.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:12.970
This was set up as a neutral zone
for both nations.

00:05:13.866 --> 00:05:15.996
Great Forest of Brandish, you say?!

00:05:16.166 --> 00:05:16.826
What is it?

00:05:17.166 --> 00:05:19.466
This is unexplored territory
no one has ever been to.

00:05:19.833 --> 00:05:23.173
This is the habitat to
unknown monsters!

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:24.800
- Are you serious?
- Yeah...

00:05:24.833 --> 00:05:31.833
That's why the Grankingdom deployed
air fleet without any ground forces.

00:05:32.166 --> 00:05:33.826
Thanks for the new information.

00:05:35.166 --> 00:05:36.596
There's no need to worry.

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:39.470
I sent out a distress signal
just before we went down.

00:05:40.033 --> 00:05:41.833
I'm sure help will come.

00:05:42.333 --> 00:05:46.533
What have you done?
They will come to kill you guys.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:48.270
I don't believe that.

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:50.400
What's the plan, Captain?

00:05:50.433 --> 00:05:53.773
Let's get out of this forest somehow
and go have some beer.

00:05:54.133 --> 00:05:56.173
The cafÃ© at Sabaru is closer.

00:05:56.333 --> 00:05:58.303
Are you telling us
to become prisoners?!

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:01.430
W-What is it?

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:05.100
W-What's the idea?!

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:14.800
Look out!

00:06:17.833 --> 00:06:20.803
Let's go to Sabaru. It's closer.

00:06:21.033 --> 00:06:22.833
We should wait for
help from our allies...

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:25.670
I'm telling you! Your allies are!

00:06:26.866 --> 00:06:29.926
We don't know if our distress signal
has been received.

00:06:30.366 --> 00:06:33.566
And we don't know if they can
afford to send out rescue vessels

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:35.230
in the middle of a fleet battle.

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:40.470
We've got lots of robot soldiers in our Army
and they are often treated as disposables.

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:43.026
It wasn't like that in
the old days, though...

00:06:43.966 --> 00:06:46.626
We have to rely on ourselves
if we want to survive.

00:06:52.266 --> 00:06:55.296
There's nothing all that great in here.
Maybe enough to have a picnic.

00:06:55.633 --> 00:06:59.233
I've got more survival skills
than an airman.

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:02.000
You aren't coming with us,
are you?

00:07:02.333 --> 00:07:06.133
I was planning to
go back to Sabaru anyway.

00:07:06.433 --> 00:07:07.603
That doesn't mean!

00:07:07.633 --> 00:07:09.033
It's okay, Deputy Officer!

00:07:10.066 --> 00:07:11.326
Let's go together.

00:07:15.566 --> 00:07:17.166
Homeron!

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:20.800
Hang on! We're going down!

00:07:20.833 --> 00:07:22.133
- What?!
- What?!

00:07:31.233 --> 00:07:32.103
Which way do we go?

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:33.500
This should be the right way.

00:07:33.933 --> 00:07:35.703
Now that's what I'd expect
from an airman.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:38.670
About what we were
talking about earlier...

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:41.730
How is General Logi
connected to this incident?

00:07:42.466 --> 00:07:47.496
The Grankingdom Army is engaged
in battle all over the world.

00:07:47.666 --> 00:07:50.896
But Logi's unit is nowhere
near the fronts.

00:07:51.666 --> 00:07:53.896
They are the Independent
Flying Squadron, after all.

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:59.630
They attacked a city of academics.
They captured several scholars from there.

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:00.770
Scholars?

00:08:01.366 --> 00:08:05.026
Yes. And he's been keeping them
on his ship ever since.

00:08:06.266 --> 00:08:11.226
It makes sense if Delphinium
took the Extra Seven to Logi.

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:13.570
What's the Extra Seven?

00:08:14.066 --> 00:08:16.696
The lost seven pages of
the Book of the Beginning.

00:08:17.766 --> 00:08:24.066
General Logi is trying to decipher
the Extra Seven behind closed doors...

00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:28.170
Is General Logi attempting
to eliminate us?

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:33.430
I don't really know what's going on
inside the Grankingdom,

00:08:33.466 --> 00:08:37.066
but it's the work of their intelligence unit...
by Delphinium.

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:42.170
Captain! This guy's words
are not worth listening to!

00:08:42.366 --> 00:08:45.126
Don't you want to know
why we're in this mess?!

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:47.870
I've lost my ship because of this!

00:08:49.266 --> 00:08:52.726
But why are you involved
in this incident?

00:08:53.533 --> 00:08:55.503
There are some kids
who are Shadow Wielders.

00:08:55.966 --> 00:08:57.896
Shadow Wielders?
Real Shadow Wielders?

00:08:58.266 --> 00:09:02.326
Yeah... They need this information.

00:09:07.866 --> 00:09:10.166
This won't be so easy to repair.

00:09:10.766 --> 00:09:11.926
No way...

00:09:12.266 --> 00:09:13.326
For what purpose?

00:09:13.433 --> 00:09:14.833
To defeat Nene.

00:09:14.866 --> 00:09:16.866
Defeat Lord Nene?!
That's never going to happen!

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:18.570
Not the way things are now.

00:09:19.333 --> 00:09:22.003
That's why I'm gathering information.

00:09:22.966 --> 00:09:27.796
To be honest, I can't go along with
Lord Nene's world domination nonsense.

00:09:28.266 --> 00:09:29.266
Captain!

00:09:29.366 --> 00:09:31.996
It's okay, Deputy Officer.
It's the same for you too, right?

00:09:32.166 --> 00:09:33.166
Well, no...

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:34.600
It's okay...

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:40.430
I'm going to look for Homeron!

00:09:41.133 --> 00:09:41.803
Shu!

00:09:42.066 --> 00:09:43.926
Then go with Marumaro.

00:09:44.366 --> 00:09:45.366
Maro?

00:09:45.500 --> 00:09:47.870
Saber Tiger can help you
with the search.

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:49.600
Maro!

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:06.830
What is this place?
This sure is a depressing forest.

00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:09.670
Shu! Get on, maro!

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:10.870
Right!

00:10:14.466 --> 00:10:15.466
I'm going too!

00:10:19.100 --> 00:10:21.770
Don't forget your way back!

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:23.570
You guys catch up with us later!

00:10:24.066 --> 00:10:25.666
Give me a break!

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:29.130
All these guys are forcing
me to do the repairs!

00:10:29.666 --> 00:10:31.196
Bouquet, hand me a screwdriver!

00:10:31.233 --> 00:10:32.233
S-Sure...

00:10:33.166 --> 00:10:35.626
No! This is a wrench!

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:38.730
S-Sorry... I didn't know!

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:09.430
It's getting quite dark.
Shall we rest for the night somewhere?

00:11:09.966 --> 00:11:12.266
I think it would be better for us
to keep moving forward.

00:11:12.533 --> 00:11:16.833
That's right. There's no way I'm spending
the night in the Brandish Woods!

00:11:17.066 --> 00:11:18.996
What's wrong, Chief Engineer?

00:11:19.433 --> 00:11:21.673
Demons come out at night in this forest!

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:24.000
Demons? Not monsters?

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:27.500
The demons catch humans
and eat them.

00:11:27.766 --> 00:11:29.066
You're kidding, right?

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:31.270
I heard it when I was a kid.

00:11:31.866 --> 00:11:35.226
Nobody who has entered
this forest at night has come back.

00:11:35.566 --> 00:11:37.666
They say they were all
eaten by the demons!

00:11:38.333 --> 00:11:42.373
You know, parents tell their kids scary stories
to keep them out of trouble, so...

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:43.500
That's not it!

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:48.370
Do you know anything about this forest?

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:52.270
Unfortunately, I've never taken on
that kind of commission before.

00:11:53.333 --> 00:11:55.503
Okay, let's move on ahead...

00:11:58.000 --> 00:11:58.670
Who's there?!

00:12:05.633 --> 00:12:06.303
Is it the wind?

00:12:07.233 --> 00:12:08.403
Okay, let's go.

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:28.100
What is it, maro?

00:12:28.933 --> 00:12:30.773
Please be careful, Marumaro.

00:12:31.466 --> 00:12:33.796
There is a presence in the area
that makes me uneasy.

00:12:49.466 --> 00:12:51.526
Are we going to walk all night?

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:53.270
We're going to walk until
we get out of this forest.

00:12:53.366 --> 00:12:54.366
All right...

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:14.600
Sergeant Major!

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:21.170
Help me!

00:13:25.466 --> 00:13:26.896
W-What were those just now?

00:13:27.333 --> 00:13:28.333
Those were Ulbacks!

00:13:28.366 --> 00:13:29.366
Ulbacks?

00:13:29.633 --> 00:13:33.203
My grandmother told me about them.
Those are the demons that eat people!

00:13:33.433 --> 00:13:34.103
After them!

00:13:34.466 --> 00:13:36.966
Too late, Captain.
They're probably eating him.

00:13:37.466 --> 00:13:40.566
Since they took him away,
there must be a nest.

00:13:41.033 --> 00:13:43.203
He'll be fed to babies
or the queen there.

00:13:43.533 --> 00:13:45.133
Do you know about them?

00:13:45.533 --> 00:13:48.333
It's what ants do.
There's no other reason.

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:49.870
Captain!

00:13:50.566 --> 00:13:52.796
Come with me!
We're going to get him back.

00:13:53.166 --> 00:13:54.596
Oh, come on.

00:13:54.766 --> 00:13:58.866
Captain! I... I don't want to go!

00:14:07.333 --> 00:14:08.333
Chief Engineer!

00:14:09.366 --> 00:14:10.366
Let go of me!

00:14:13.033 --> 00:14:14.333
N-No way!

00:14:17.800 --> 00:14:21.870
H-Help me, Captain!

00:14:25.133 --> 00:14:28.233
There's no way we can save them!
At this rate, they'll get us, too!

00:14:28.633 --> 00:14:31.533
I can't abandon my crew.

00:14:35.833 --> 00:14:36.503
It's coming.

00:14:48.566 --> 00:14:52.296
Let's go! Blue Dragon!

00:14:57.266 --> 00:14:58.426
Minotaur!

00:14:58.466 --> 00:14:59.466
Coming!

00:15:04.033 --> 00:15:05.773
What're you guys?!

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:07.470
Go home now!

00:15:10.866 --> 00:15:12.796
You've sure got guts!

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:14.630
W-What?

00:15:14.666 --> 00:15:16.926
They're probably after you guys.

00:15:16.966 --> 00:15:18.066
Why's that, maro?!

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:21.570
Please be careful.
They intend to eat all of you.

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:22.670
What?!

00:15:25.366 --> 00:15:27.366
You jerk!

00:15:28.466 --> 00:15:29.866
You little!

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:41.670
What's this?

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:46.670
There they are!

00:15:52.833 --> 00:15:55.273
Let's part ways here,
Master Informant.

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:56.800
What do you mean?

00:15:57.066 --> 00:16:01.026
I'm going to save my crew.
But that's not necessary for you.

00:16:01.666 --> 00:16:03.226
After coming this far?
I don't think so.

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:07.530
You've got your own people
you must save, right?

00:16:08.066 --> 00:16:08.726
Yeah...

00:16:08.966 --> 00:16:13.026
It's okay. Let's do what we need to do.
See you around.

00:16:13.966 --> 00:16:14.626
Hold it!

00:16:15.400 --> 00:16:18.300
I wouldn't be able to face Shu
if I abandon you guys.

00:16:18.700 --> 00:16:19.370
Shu?

00:16:19.533 --> 00:16:21.073
He's a Shadow Wielder kid...

00:16:21.933 --> 00:16:23.333
He must be quite a guy...

00:16:23.833 --> 00:16:25.173
Yeah, that's right.

00:16:29.166 --> 00:16:29.826
Go!

00:16:46.166 --> 00:16:47.526
That was a close one.

00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:49.870
What?!

00:16:50.333 --> 00:16:51.003
Over there!

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:05.100
You little!

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:20.800
Captain!

00:17:21.666 --> 00:17:22.666
Captain!

00:17:28.333 --> 00:17:30.133
Damn it... This can't be how it ends!

00:17:31.766 --> 00:17:32.996
Oh! That was!

00:17:36.433 --> 00:17:38.033
Homeron!

00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:39.370
Shu!

00:17:40.133 --> 00:17:41.873
Go, Blue Dragon!

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:51.800
You're in my way!

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:53.570
Move!

00:17:54.033 --> 00:17:56.033
You little!

00:17:57.266 --> 00:17:59.696
Shadows are incredible for sure.

00:18:00.133 --> 00:18:03.973
I come here to confirm the death of
Norg crew members, and look who I find.

00:18:04.533 --> 00:18:05.533
To confirm?

00:18:05.833 --> 00:18:08.933
No, you came to finish them off,
right, Delphinium?!

00:18:09.433 --> 00:18:13.633
I never thought you'd be here...
I suppose I'll give you credit for that.

00:18:14.433 --> 00:18:18.103
The captain of the Norg told me
everything before he died.

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:21.100
The most important information
was regarding General Logi.

00:18:21.533 --> 00:18:24.773
But that information will die here.

00:18:24.966 --> 00:18:27.226
So your mission will be complete
after you kill me?

00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:31.300
That's right. I don't need to
fight that Shadow Wielder.

00:18:43.133 --> 00:18:46.233
The information will never
reach those kids.

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:49.400
Shu!

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:52.630
Homeron!

00:18:53.133 --> 00:18:54.133
Shu!

00:19:25.966 --> 00:19:26.626
Shu...

00:19:32.733 --> 00:19:33.733
Hang in there, okay?

00:19:39.066 --> 00:19:40.226
Homeron!

00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:44.600
Hold it!

00:19:48.900 --> 00:19:49.930
Damn it!

00:19:51.233 --> 00:19:52.333
Blue Dragon!

00:20:40.133 --> 00:20:41.133
Shu...

00:20:41.500 --> 00:20:42.530
Is Homeron?

00:20:50.166 --> 00:20:56.666
That...woman killed Homeron.
She is Delphinium!

00:21:06.566 --> 00:21:07.926
Help... Help...

00:21:08.366 --> 00:21:10.266
Get me out of here...

00:21:16.333 --> 00:21:17.003
It's sticky.

00:21:20.333 --> 00:21:22.903
Thank you. You saved us.

00:21:23.233 --> 00:21:26.103
Are you a Grankingdom soldier,
maro?

00:21:27.033 --> 00:21:28.403
Are you the crew of the Norg?

00:21:29.066 --> 00:21:32.596
That's right...
Are you Shu, by any chance?

00:21:33.266 --> 00:21:35.596
No... Shu's over there.

00:21:44.600 --> 00:21:45.800
Are you Shu?

00:21:49.600 --> 00:21:54.830
That master informant
talked highly about you...

00:21:57.600 --> 00:22:01.400
I'll tell you the information he was
going to tell you in his place.

00:22:04.166 --> 00:22:08.226
The Extra Seven is now inside
General Logi's battleship!

00:22:10.633 --> 00:22:11.933
Did you say General Logi?!

00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:12.770
Maro...

00:22:13.200 --> 00:22:15.730
Logi is now trying to decipher it.

00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:18.900
General Logi!

00:22:19.766 --> 00:22:22.696
He lied about our deaths.

00:22:23.166 --> 00:22:26.226
Whether or not Delphinium
believed it was a gamble.

00:22:27.133 --> 00:22:30.103
And you guys have won that gamble.

00:22:31.333 --> 00:22:32.333
Homeron!

00:22:35.633 --> 00:22:36.633
Thank you.

00:24:20.233 --> 00:24:22.733
Shu and the others head off
to recover the Extra Seven,

00:24:22.766 --> 00:24:24.826
but Gilliam and others, now more
powerful than ever, stand before them.

00:24:24.900 --> 00:24:27.000
They're more powerful?
Has something changed?

00:24:27.033 --> 00:24:29.603
As his rival,
he can't deceive my eyes, maro.

00:24:29.733 --> 00:24:31.503
It's his glass lenses, maro.

00:24:31.533 --> 00:24:32.533
I can see it, too.

00:24:32.733 --> 00:24:34.273
That old lady is wearing
sexy underwear!

00:24:34.300 --> 00:24:35.300
Maro!

00:24:35.333 --> 00:24:38.373
Next on Blue Dragon:
Versus The Independent Flying Squadron
